        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Christian democracy</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 1891 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Thinkers</span><span class="info-stat-val">Jacques Maritain, who comes closest to a leading thinker and tried to reconcile democracy and human rights with Thomist natural law; Emmanuel Mounier, linked to personalism; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-leo-xiii">Pope Leo XIII</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-pius-xi">Pope Pius XI</a>; Heinrich Pesch, of solidarism; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abraham-kuyper">Abraham Kuyper</a>, the neo-Calvinist founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anti-revolutionary-party">Anti-Revolutionary Party</a>; Luigi Sturzo, of popularism; Frédéric Ozanam and Wilhelm von Ketteler, early social Catholics</span></div>
